content:
{
  "asset": "P-201 - Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531. Reported chemical leakage at the diaphragm/head at approximately 2 drops per second; motor reported running normally.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Leak reading: approximately 2 drops per second at the diaphragm/head. No allowable leakage rate or diaphragm-leak limit for a Velatek VX-90 is provided, so this reading cannot be classified against a numeric limit. The AquaDyne HF-300 bearing-temperature limits and vibration zones are not applicable leak limits for P-201. P1 and stop-now are conservative work-order decisions for confirmed, ongoing chemical loss of containment, not a claim that a documented leak threshold has been exceeded.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor condition: 'running normally' is qualitative; no motor current, speed, temperature, pressure or vibration reading is reported. The HF-300 rating of 1480 rpm, 55 kW and 400 V and its bearing-housing limits of normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C and trip 90 C do not apply to the Velatek motor/pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The two specific SSP-07 condition triggers cannot be evaluated from this report: there is no vibration reading in the manufacturer's highest severity zone and no bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit. The HF-300 Zone D range of 7.1-11.0 mm/s RMS and 80 C alarm are not P-201 limits. Consequently, neither SSP-07's vibration stop/reliability-engineer rule nor its bearing-temperature P1 rule is the basis for this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Undetermined beyond loss of sealing integrity at the reported diaphragm/head location. The report does not establish whether the diaphragm itself, its seating, or another head joint has failed. The HF-300 troubleshooting causes of worn/cracked mechanical-seal faces, dry running and shaft misalignment concern shaft-seal leakage on a different pump and must not be used as the diagnosis for P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-201 as a precaution for the active chemical leak and prevent operation until the leak has been repaired and an applicable restart check has been completed. This is not an application of the HF-300 vibration-zone stop criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head or working on its sealing components, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the line; then obtain the line-break permit. SSP-07 applies site-wide to pumps, and the work order must list the applicable controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves as the documented minimum controls for chemical-line work. Before line break, confirm the actual chemical and its safety requirements; do not assume sodium hypochlorite, which C16 identifies specifically for P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only after isolation, draining, venting and permitting, inspect the diaphragm/head area to confirm the leak source and identify damaged components. Hold strip-down, replacement and reassembly instructions pending the Velatek VX-90 procedure for serial VX-5531; do not substitute the HF-300 mechanical-seal replacement, alignment procedure or fastener torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not assign a seal-gland torque to P-201 from the supplied documents. Neither the HF-300 Table 5 value of 25 Nm nor service-bulletin value of 30 Nm applies to this Velatek diaphragm pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Verify component mass before any lift. If a component exceeds 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. Do not assume P-201 has a 68 kg assembly; that mass belongs to the HF-300 back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Mandatory for internal pump/sealing work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required by the cited chemical-line control. Chemical identity and any additional chemical-specific protection remain to be confirmed rather than inferred from the sodium-hypochlorite duty of P-101 to P-106.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional lifting control: a signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment are required only if the component to be lifted is heavier than 25 kg; no P-201 component mass is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Technician scope can be planned for shutdown/isolation support, permit-controlled inspection and identification of the failed components. No evidence-based crew size or repair duration can be set until the chemical controls, Velatek procedure and required parts are known.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "HF-300 seal torque/part conflict: manual parts information identifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead requires cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; pumps below that serial continue with HF3-450 and Table 5. Decision for this asset: neither option applies, because P-201 is a Velatek VX-90 with serial VX-5531, outside both the HF-300 model and HF3 serial-range scope. No P-201 torque or seal part is therefore specified.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Model-applicability decision: the remaining AquaDyne operating limits, exploded assembly/parts information, troubleshooting and maintenance procedures are for the HF-300, not the reported Velatek VX-90. Exclude the HF-300 68 kg lifting assumption, bearing/vibration limits, mechanical-seal diagnosis, replacement sequence and alignment tolerances from P-201's repair plan.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C04",
        "C05",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What chemical, concentration and SDS apply at P-201, and what additional PPE, exposure controls, drain/vent disposal arrangements or spill response are required? C16 identifies sodium hypochlorite only for P-101 to P-106, while C15 provides only generic chemical-line goggles and nitrile-glove controls. [C15, C16]",
    "What does the Velatek VX-90 manual for serial VX-5531 specify for permissible leakage, diaphragm/head disassembly, inspection, replacement, fastener torques, pressure/leak testing and restart? None of the supplied HF-300 procedures or limits answers these points. [C02, C07, C09, C10, C11]",
    "What are the correct diaphragm, head-seal and any other required part numbers and quantities? The HF-300 parts list and HF3-450/HF3-450B bulletin cannot be used for this asset. [C05, C13]",
    "Does any P-201 component exceed 25 kg and therefore require the conditional lifting plan and certified lifting equipment? No Velatek component mass is provided. [C15]",
    "What site rule formally assigns priority and shutdown classification to a chemical leak of approximately 2 drops per second? C15 documents an immediate-stop rule for highest-zone vibration and a P1 rule for bearing temperature above alarm, but no chemical-leak threshold; P1 and stop-now here are interim conservative decisions requiring operations/safety confirmation. [C15]"
  ]
}
